#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105520 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e964b6-4cdd-56c8-b63d-95b29bec5809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326495} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac9f39d-1e76-5ac0-ae9b-161f2e81b5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326496} {:answer/id #uuid "d689606a-b1d6-5a47-96a7-8235a9f0c345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326497} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f97eb6-6e15-5c61-a786-93ddc8911b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326498} {:answer/id #uuid "91517ee9-d156-547e-8050-cdec91a0f02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22e964b6-4cdd-56c8-b63d-95b29bec5809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a574109-36b8-5949-9b70-4eeaf13c2197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c59800e-2701-5f60-8d3e-288359179eb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128421" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975a10d8-e0f9-5167-b382-47e92eb34088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304797} {:answer/id #uuid "0b9914a3-6baf-52f5-b2b7-3c9ee7144a72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304798} {:answer/id #uuid "291a9c56-c12a-54ce-b94a-8ec1c044442d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304799} {:answer/id #uuid "01db86c0-0f6a-5292-8cd0-6a439b395459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304800} {:answer/id #uuid "06de81d2-3e21-557f-9a3a-8ac7735e68bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975a10d8-e0f9-5167-b382-47e92eb34088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304797} :answer-field/id #uuid "47d5fb1f-490d-55ae-985d-d4129fc0807b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fee03e2-7b8b-52e8-9d97-0baaa37f0e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128436" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "673cae1d-eb32-571c-b27a-757d2ebd1e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326502} {:answer/id #uuid "d4abd956-3995-5eb0-9bf2-c9c45b45d748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326503} {:answer/id #uuid "e25bf302-b77e-57bd-8563-b8e1ff3e6927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326504} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4b2da7-fc1c-5d45-b5d1-66c133668f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326505} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bf8f1b-bae9-5ea5-9fe5-ca22e4d3cea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "673cae1d-eb32-571c-b27a-757d2ebd1e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326502} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1ae912-933b-5c96-971e-c28e417ab097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc223040-3a37-576b-a678-9d3b00321dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-18259" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13659ae6-e567-53cb-9aab-761952bceac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326509} {:answer/id #uuid "5b76fa60-842d-5b16-8204-99b6ff005fc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13659ae6-e567-53cb-9aab-761952bceac9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326509} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0cd9b70-e2f1-54e9-9ff7-5f2bc5f704cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd47ad71-726b-598c-9cd8-8f7ef7e44966" :question/math-academy-id "q-275353" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$, $b=⟨-1,k,2⟩$, and $c=⟨3,-2,4⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & k \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(k\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-8k-8+10-6+9k \\\\  & =k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ k-4 & =0 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef5ebf59-6fe5-59ef-a3d3-b0c347a63905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304832} {:answer/id #uuid "39d7c572-9876-5c6c-83ec-04cbeb3e08a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef5ebf59-6fe5-59ef-a3d3-b0c347a63905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304832} :answer-field/id #uuid "839829d8-fa02-5da6-a1dd-b573f71f9cd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0744b7bb-a8e1-5df9-b653-93a21c6bbd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-280670" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcdef9cd-da53-54f7-b9b4-1dc1d0848e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcdef9cd-da53-54f7-b9b4-1dc1d0848e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326513} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ddc02b8-3a95-5c91-b1c2-e5d366fdbe06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d369a6bd-35ca-5c57-9419-5c24b72446a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-280720" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf549120-6114-5feb-b848-f01439d29d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326516} {:answer/id #uuid "45d1db52-a301-5925-a6a6-997e7f782f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf549120-6114-5feb-b848-f01439d29d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326516} :answer-field/id #uuid "e414834f-173d-5fbb-bb6a-4f2a12084f4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "875a18b4-72a0-591f-b9da-03167f35bd1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280722" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "519fd9e0-4bf0-51e6-9a98-5ea8ab551b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "519fd9e0-4bf0-51e6-9a98-5ea8ab551b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326520} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5833afc-d2f4-5d52-b7a8-e6659db0c2c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0731c398-d5f2-578b-97ec-94db7b1c6288" :question/math-academy-id "q-281025" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,2),$ $B(5,1,3),$ $C(4,3,5),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5i+1j+3k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =3k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)-1(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)+1(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(9)-1(3)+1(0) \\\\  & =18-3+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b421de7-6ce3-531e-ab76-200c91231136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b421de7-6ce3-531e-ab76-200c91231136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304851} :answer-field/id #uuid "9987a9a4-b325-596d-b143-3f3c5385e5c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90129f6e-2010-58a8-9c15-bbe333617408" :question/math-academy-id "q-281030" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c615b6-22b7-56af-a72a-dd2339cfde92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326523} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecf3894-0b3a-5cbc-a9fd-f9405c012274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326524} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9dbd75-1207-5c9d-b7af-52d043d2ba3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326525} {:answer/id #uuid "fecbdbfd-7093-5809-9a05-43b41ec72c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326526} {:answer/id #uuid "15db8fd3-a04e-5dbd-b62c-8c9c88d84d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15db8fd3-a04e-5dbd-b62c-8c9c88d84d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326527} :answer-field/id #uuid "00d97457-7080-5315-ab17-df1a145f1cc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d563b67f-cff3-5de6-b840-59edf3c18de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40221" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-5,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,1,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)-3(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)+0 \\\\  & =25+6 \\\\  & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|31|=31.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "add6a24a-4d07-5314-a478-1762592e98b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326530} {:answer/id #uuid "ec835b57-b746-5d80-9ba2-9c5230f8d1a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326531} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fda1c7-dbbf-5848-92c8-87c11f36f660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326532} {:answer/id #uuid "1f8ea925-5c7c-5162-a7cb-d46308fa2426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326533} {:answer/id #uuid "506feec1-8f45-571f-9702-238851de28ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8ea925-5c7c-5162-a7cb-d46308fa2426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326533} :answer-field/id #uuid "11449c7d-9008-5a04-b273-7f8f825ddaf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "258d49ee-e16c-5cac-8f15-2e4bb377a507" :question/math-academy-id "q-42048" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,2,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $c=⟨4,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)-2(3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2k-2+6 \\\\  & =-2k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -2k+4 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =4 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81fb8ddc-f318-5698-818f-36a48f3da9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326537} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0b5e85-44cb-557e-9206-9a37087a8708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326538} {:answer/id #uuid "d29093a6-9bbf-5e1f-9b1c-b204bc15c666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326539} {:answer/id #uuid "28353255-7392-53a2-adc7-d8a24ed1c5c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326540} {:answer/id #uuid "c491227b-4068-593a-ba43-4a57916592b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d29093a6-9bbf-5e1f-9b1c-b204bc15c666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326539} :answer-field/id #uuid "a80dfce7-2939-52cf-a682-e51cb10d73e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72581fd8-6374-573b-9323-94b487681bf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42050" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 1)+2(2\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-22+20+4 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a92c1fc-1f6a-52c1-a15b-f8e954164b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326544} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc9b0e-3bab-5844-af84-e4c571c2be33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326545} {:answer/id #uuid "804b614d-6206-5873-be9e-e700c6f4ef7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326546} {:answer/id #uuid "f8035a13-8cb2-5534-a42a-f98c2dc86b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326547} {:answer/id #uuid "0558ff42-1be5-5630-9918-2d6b027d7b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57bc9b0e-3bab-5844-af84-e4c571c2be33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326545} :answer-field/id #uuid "52ff9321-5cc5-50d9-98cd-77b72128c0a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "287f03d9-5f5b-5d4e-a5e1-a25d62c26b2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73744" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,1,0)$, $B(-2,1,0)$, $C(3,2,0)$, and $D(1,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =-3i \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+1j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+3k)-(i+j) \\\\  & =3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)-0+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55b15b82-55b6-567a-b3c1-a2387a37ec7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326551} {:answer/id #uuid "5a768aad-4442-5eeb-b551-844df002bec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326552} {:answer/id #uuid "2e28d937-852d-5f0c-bb97-15536aedf7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326553} {:answer/id #uuid "ed28cc46-223b-5dd5-8282-3e2fc22b7f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326554} {:answer/id #uuid "3df06724-6af5-531c-aec9-9679c50c5365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a768aad-4442-5eeb-b551-844df002bec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326552} :answer-field/id #uuid "1754209c-d9d5-5402-a2c6-523ddaed3744" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e77cbb8-c0a3-501c-a9ea-9b64ed425d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-73746" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(0,1,2)$, $B(-1,0,1)$, $C(1,1,0)$, and $D(3,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =i-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =4+7+2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|13|=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "257928ef-38b0-5bb3-8d46-b148c8a0fb6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326558} {:answer/id #uuid "f2faa3ae-9029-5ee5-ad41-157ffd70ee23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326559} {:answer/id #uuid "c6267406-f129-5442-870e-e361a1704593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326560} {:answer/id #uuid "5120e02e-84c2-54be-a3a5-47faf6f67746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326561} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d7f9b4-9327-538e-a2ef-4fcc30109020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6267406-f129-5442-870e-e361a1704593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326560} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d620a61-306c-538e-8d78-68b351e16a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "273efc02-510a-5322-a187-ba8e3b597f41" :question/math-academy-id "q-73753" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-2,1,1)$, $B(2,1,0)$, $C(1,-1,2)$, and $D(3,-2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =4i-k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j-2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =5i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot (-3))-0-(3\\cdot (-3)-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =36-1 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$"}]}
